     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;arial narrow&quot;,sans-serif\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br clear=\"all\"></font></div><div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial narrow, sans-serif\">Hello, </font></div><div class=\"gmail_default\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial narrow, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div class=\"gmail_default\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial narrow, sans-serif\">I&#39;m try to explore RRPP package, i want to runn the examples with a mixed model using <span>PupfishHeads data: </span></font></div><div class=\"gmail_default\"><span><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial narrow, sans-serif\"><span><br></span></font></span></div><div class=\"gmail_default\"><span><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial narrow, sans-serif\"><span>PupfishHeads</span><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">$</span><span>logHeadSize &lt;- </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">log</span><span>(PupfishHeads</span><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">$</span><span>headSize)<br>fit &lt;- </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">lm.rrpp</span><span>(logHeadSize </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">~ </span><span>sex </span><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">+ </span><span>locality</span><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">/</span><span>year,<br></span><span>SS.type = </span><span>&quot;I&quot;</span><span>, </span><span>data = </span><span>PupfishHeads,<br></span><span>print.progress = </span><span>FALSE</span><span>)<br></span><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">summary</span><span>(fit)</span>  <br style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:-webkit-auto\"></font></span></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"color:rgb(11,83,148)\"><font face=\"arial narrow, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div class=\"gmail_default\"><span><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial narrow, sans-serif\">but despite the linear model run and  i got results, the next messsage appear:</font></span></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"color:rgb(11,83,148)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(79,153,5)\"><font face=\"arial narrow, sans-serif\"><br></font></span></div><div class=\"gmail_default\"><span><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial narrow, sans-serif\"><b>Warning: Because variables in the linear model are redundant <br>the linear model design has been truncated (via QR decomposition).<br>Original X columns: 13<br>Final X columns (rank): 9<br>Check coefficients or degrees of freedom in ANOVA to see changes.<br></b></font></span></div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial narrow, sans-serif\"><span class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"color:rgb(11,83,148)\"><b></b></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial narrow, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial narrow, sans-serif\"><span class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;arial narrow&quot;,sans-serif\">However  I am using package data, </span>somebod<span class=\"gmail_default\">y</span> <span class=\"gmail_default\">know if that is a error from the package? </span><span class=\"gmail_default\"></span><br></font></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial narrow, sans-serif\"><span class=\"gmail_default\"><br></span></font></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial narrow, sans-serif\"><span class=\"gmail_default\">thank you!!</span></font></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial narrow, sans-serif\"><span class=\"gmail_default\"><br></span></font></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span class=\"gmail_default\"><font face=\"arial narrow, sans-serif\">Ana</font></span><div dir=\"ltr\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><br></font><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><font size=\"2\" color=\"#0c343d\" style=\"font-s